      "source_revision": "d902041c348b199d1dd2de5ab73de24ff5a26e67",
      "content": "# Porto Whitepaper\n\nThis repository contains the canonical Porto whitepaper: **\"Porto: A Network-Owned Infrastructure Layer for Music Distribution.\"**\n\nPorto is decentralized streaming infrastructure that replaces platform-owned delivery and settlement with a network run by artists, labels, publishers, and independent node operators. Every play is logged on Porto Chain, a purpose-built blockchain, and settled automatically on-chain , replacing a 90–180 day intermediary payout chain with same-epoch, auditable settlement.\n\n## Contents\n\n- [`porto-whitepaper.md`](./porto-whitepaper.md) , the full paper, covering:\n  1. Introduction , what Porto is and isn't\n  2. The Problem , opacity, delay, and margin extraction in current streaming royalties\n  3. The Porto Network , system overview and participant roles\n  4. Porto Chain , the app-chain architecture\n  5. PRT , the token model\n  6. Streaming and stream accounting\n  7. Payouts , the settlement model\n  8. Governance\n  9. Phased rollout, from Beta to permissionless mainnet\n  10. Market position\n  11. Team\n  12. Conclusion\n\nNormative technical specifications, written in an EIP/RFC-style format, live separately in the Porto Improvement Proposal (PIP) series (`../pips/`) and are referenced throughout the paper.\n\n## Status\n\n**v0.1.0 , Draft.**\n\n## Copyright and licence\n\nCopyright © 2026 Entropy Tech Ltd.\n\nThe whitepaper is licensed under the [Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Porto names, logos, and other trademarks are not licensed under this licence.\n\n## Author\n\nRichard Melkonian, Porto Labs\n"
